{"id": "EUVD-2026-91469", "enisaUuid": "b8f61dd1-8508-3c4f-a3ff-50c04f750081", "description": "YesWiki before 4.6.7 contains a server-side request forgery vulnerability in validateKeyIdUrl() that allows unauthenticated attackers to bypass the SSRF guard using 6to4, NAT64, or IPv4-compatible IPv6 addresses. Attackers can send a crafted Signature keyId to the public actor inbox route to reach cloud metadata, loopback services, or internal hosts.", "datePublished": "2026-10-02T11:38:27", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-02T14:10:28", "baseScore": 8.3, "baseScoreVersion": "4.0", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:4.0/AV:N/AC:H/AT:P/PR:N/UI:N/VC:H/VI:L/VA:N/SC:N/SI:N/SA:N", "references": ["https://github.com/YesWiki/yeswiki/security/advisories/GHSA-85f2-5r47-2pwm", "https://www.vulncheck.com/advisories/yeswiki-before-4.6.7-ssrf-guard-bypass-via-ipv6-transition-addresses"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-104458", "GHSA-gg34-f95q-rfgp"], "assigner": "VulnCheck", "epss": 0.32, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "096be4fc-edbc-3d88-92f8-16b77df3818c", "product": {"name": "yeswiki", "vendor": {"name": "YesWiki"}}, "product_version": "0 <4.6.7"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "667d5d4b-4952-339a-b9c5-66642daa226d", "vendor": {"name": "YesWiki"}}], "isExploited": false}